Kind: ablation
Issue: #964
Takes out: the reading of a module's declaration: module_read() never looks for the .uros_drives section, and the HAL takes every module of a pool for one that declares nothing, as a HAL that never found the section would.  Once "/" is served, the network card's line says no module of net, in the bundle or on the disk, declares it, where chora_probe, on the disk, declares the card by its vendor and device; and no chora is started on it.
Run: --iommu intel --edu --entry 68 600 -smp 4
Expect: hal: [0-9a-f]{2}:[0-9a-f]{2}\.[0-7] 8086:(100e|10d3) class 0200[0-9a-f]{2}: no module of net, in the bundle or on the disk, declares it

